# Versioned support claims

Before changing `packages/schema`, `packages/compiler`, `packages/runtime`, `packages/canvas-renderer`, `packages/motionscript-emitter`, `packages/format-lottie`, `packages/format-svg`, `packages/format-import-core`, `packages/round-trip`, or `docs/languages`:

1. Read `packages/schema/capabilities/releases.json`.
2. Read the current MotionScript and Scene IR version files it names.
3. Read `docs/languages/compatibility-policy.md` and the root `AGENTS.md`.

Published version files are immutable. Support claims change only together with the registry, tests, and the pending or new version entry. Evaluation reports describe one revision; they are not the specification.

There is no V1 feature ceiling. Add Scene IR and MotionScript capabilities needed to render modern Lottie and SVG. Path morph, mattes, animated paint, and repeater/merge are in that set. Stop for a design decision only for a new execution model, such as loops or function declarations.
